I've tested this with a concrete PHP script, and the issue is still reproducible on the latest development build.

Here is the code I'm using to clear the Redis cache:

```php
function flushRedisCache($cache): bool
{
    $iterator     = null;
    $keysToDelete = [];

    do {
        $previousIterator = $iterator;
        $keys             = $cache->scan($iterator, '*', 1000);

        if ($keys !== false && ! empty($keys)) {
            foreach ($keys as $key) {
                $keysToDelete[] = $key;
            }
        }

        if ($keys === false && $iterator === $previousIterator && $iterator !== 0) {
            throw new RuntimeException(
                'Redis SCAN failed: iterator did not advance.'
            );
        }
    } while ((int) $iterator !== 0);

    foreach (array_chunk($keysToDelete, 500) as $batch) {
        $deleted = $cache->del(...$batch);

        if ($deleted === false) {
            throw new RuntimeException('Redis DEL failed.');
        }
    }

    return true;
}

echo "Flush cache in progress...<br>";

try {
    flushRedisCache($cache);
    echo "Cache flushed successfully.";
} catch (RuntimeException $e) {
    echo "Error flushing cache: " . $e->getMessage();
}
```

